('cf467399-f55f-49e4-8734-a8b87c1043a7', 'en', 'Peel potatoes and cut them into 1/2-inch slices. Place in a pot and cover with water; bring to a boil. Boil for 2 minutes, then drain and set aside.'),
('cf467399-f55f-49e4-8734-a8b87c1043a7', 'ko', 'Peel potatoes and cut them into 1/2-inch slices. Place in a pot and cover with water; bring to a boil. Boil for 2 minutes, then drain and set aside.'),
('7b864d85-5cea-4dc7-8837-934c59fb68c4', 'en', 'Heat a large oven-proof skillet over medium-high heat. Pour in olive oil, then add onions. Sauté until lightly caramelized, 8 to 10 minutes. Stir in garlic and sauté until onions are deep brown and garlic is soft. Transfer mixture to a bowl.'),
('7b864d85-5cea-4dc7-8837-934c59fb68c4', 'ko', 'Heat a large oven-proof skillet over medium-high heat. Pour in olive oil, then add onions. Sauté until lightly caramelized, 8 to 10 minutes. Stir in garlic and sauté until onions are deep brown and garlic is soft. Transfer mixture to a bowl.'),
('0f2d2122-3462-41e6-84c7-c69b229a0246', 'en', 'Place the skillet back on the stove over low heat. Melt butter in the skillet, then cover the bottom with 1/3 of the potatoes. Season with salt and pepper. Cover potatoes with 1/2 of the onion mixture. Cover with 1/2 of the remaining potatoes; season with salt and pepper. Spread remaining onion mixture on top. Cover with remaining potatoes; season with salt and pepper.'),
('0f2d2122-3462-41e6-84c7-c69b229a0246', 'ko', 'Place the skillet back on the stove over low heat. Melt butter in the skillet, then cover the bottom with 1/3 of the potatoes. Season with salt and pepper. Cover potatoes with 1/2 of the onion mixture. Cover with 1/2 of the remaining potatoes; season with salt and pepper. Spread remaining onion mixture on top. Cover with remaining potatoes; season with salt and pepper.'),
('e0ade299-d885-4481-8307-c14994dad132', 'en', 'Bake in the preheated oven until potatoes are tender and browned on top, 10 to 12 minutes.'),
('e0ade299-d885-4481-8307-c14994dad132', 'ko', 'Bake in the preheated oven until potatoes are tender and browned on top, 10 to 12 minutes.'),
('b30e029e-f5cb-44a5-8596-197e3fb4c3ec', 'en', 'Use a spatula to transfer potatoes to a serving platter. Sprinkle with chopped parsley just before serving.'),
('b30e029e-f5cb-44a5-8596-197e3fb4c3ec', 'ko', 'Use a spatula to transfer potatoes to a serving platter. Sprinkle with chopped parsley just before serving.'),
('ff69f0f7-ab78-444e-8bbf-4c28d8368458', 'en', 'Soak dried salted cod in cold water for 24 hours, changing the water several times.'),
('ff69f0f7-ab78-444e-8bbf-4c28d8368458', 'ko', 'Soak dried salted cod in cold water for 24 hours, changing the water several times.'),
('ca26443e-fb0b-4c8b-895d-25136515014c', 'en', 'Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add soaked cod; boil until flakes easily with a fork, about 5 minutes. Transfer cod to a cutting board; save water for cooking potatoes. Remove cod skin and bones then flake the meat into pieces using a fork; set aside in a large bowl.'),
('ca26443e-fb0b-4c8b-895d-25136515014c', 'ko', 'Bring a large pot of water to a boil. Add soaked cod; boil until flakes easily with a fork, about 5 minutes. Transfer cod to a cutting board; save water for cooking potatoes. Remove cod skin and bones then flake the meat into pieces using a fork; set aside in a large bowl.'),
('d35efff7-5fdd-49af-863f-c13ecc1ab637', 'en', 'Whisk olive oil, 1 tablespoon parsley, 1 clove garlic, pepper flakes, and black pepper together in a small bowl; pour over cod and lightly toss to coat.'),
('d35efff7-5fdd-49af-863f-c13ecc1ab637', 'ko', 'Whisk olive oil, 1 tablespoon parsley, 1 clove garlic, pepper flakes, and black pepper together in a small bowl; pour over cod and lightly toss to coat.'),
('5ec38ea2-1641-40e9-8d45-7d02c35437d1', 'en', 'Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Grease an 8x11-inch baking dish.'),
('5ec38ea2-1641-40e9-8d45-7d02c35437d1', 'ko', 'Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Grease an 8x11-inch baking dish.'),
('ea0c9419-6716-4afe-8796-691e19b97768', 'en', 'Place potatoes in reserved pot salt cod cooking water; bring to a boil. Cook until tender, about 20 minutes. Drain under cool water, peel, and cut into 1/4-inch slices.'),
('ea0c9419-6716-4afe-8796-691e19b97768', 'ko', 'Place potatoes in reserved pot salt cod cooking water; bring to a boil. Cook until tender, about 20 minutes. Drain under cool water, peel, and cut into 1/4-inch slices.'),
('c399b156-f8bb-4c83-8775-5dcd4aad7b95', 'en', 'While potatoes cook, melt butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onions; sauté until golden and caramelized. Stir in remaining 1 clove garlic; set aside.'),
('c399b156-f8bb-4c83-8775-5dcd4aad7b95', 'ko', 'While potatoes cook, melt butter in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onions; sauté until golden and caramelized. Stir in remaining 1 clove garlic; set aside.'),
('a8cd9f98-c3b9-4c6a-8a36-e22107bf1587', 'en', 'Layer 1/2 of the potatoes in the bottom of the prepared baking dish; cover with 1/2 of the cod, then 1/2 of the onions. Repeat layers, ending with onions.'),
('a8cd9f98-c3b9-4c6a-8a36-e22107bf1587', 'ko', 'Layer 1/2 of the potatoes in the bottom of the prepared baking dish; cover with 1/2 of the cod, then 1/2 of the onions. Repeat layers, ending with onions.'),
('8250f82f-b442-4b9b-83bd-e4fb3197f71e', 'en', 'Bake in the preheated oven until lightly browned, about 15 minutes. Garnish with olives and hard-cooked eggs; sprinkle with remaining 7 tablespoons parsley.'),
('8250f82f-b442-4b9b-83bd-e4fb3197f71e', 'ko', 'Bake in the preheated oven until lightly browned, about 15 minutes. Garnish with olives and hard-cooked eggs; sprinkle with remaining 7 tablespoons parsley.'),
('1544425e-28bb-4b4c-8893-42206af866f0', 'en', 'Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Place green peppers in a baking dish with 1/8 cup water in the bottom.'),
('1544425e-28bb-4b4c-8893-42206af866f0', 'ko', 'Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Place green peppers in a baking dish with 1/8 cup water in the bottom.'),
('87c7a370-4eb7-44e1-8ff7-59e3b588cec3', 'en', 'Bake in the preheated oven until peppers are slightly browned around the edges, 20 to 25 minutes.'),
('87c7a370-4eb7-44e1-8ff7-59e3b588cec3', 'ko', 'Bake in the preheated oven until peppers are slightly browned around the edges, 20 to 25 minutes.'),
('951cd2bd-24da-4930-8cc9-71383d6058d1', 'en', 'While the peppers are baking, whisk 1/4 cup water and 2 tablespoons taco seasoning together in a small bowl. Add chicken and toss to coat. Cover the bowl with plastic wrap and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 15 minutes.'),
('951cd2bd-24da-4930-8cc9-71383d6058d1', 'ko', 'While the peppers are baking, whisk 1/4 cup water and 2 tablespoons taco seasoning together in a small bowl. Add chicken and toss to coat. Cover the bowl with plastic wrap and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 15 minutes.'),
('7d3d502e-6271-4235-8f9c-fddf307067c4', 'en', 'Combine remaining 1 cup water and rice in a pot over high heat; bring to a boil. Cover, reduce heat to low, and cook for 15 minutes. Remove from the heat. Stir in remaining taco seasoning and let sit, covered, until tender, about 15 minutes more. Remove the lid, drain any remaining liquid, and set aside.'),
('7d3d502e-6271-4235-8f9c-fddf307067c4', 'ko', 'Combine remaining 1 cup water and rice in a pot over high heat; bring to a boil. Cover, reduce heat to low, and cook for 15 minutes. Remove from the heat. Stir in remaining taco seasoning and let sit, covered, until tender, about 15 minutes more. Remove the lid, drain any remaining liquid, and set aside.'),
('9434ed57-612a-4d4b-81ca-6fc4dff5ff65', 'en', 'Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.'),
('9434ed57-612a-4d4b-81ca-6fc4dff5ff65', 'ko', 'Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.'),
('5af34424-4c7e-481a-842a-26fc4e284881', 'en', 'Remove chicken from the refrigerator and place on the preheated grill with the pepper slices. Cook chicken until no longer pink in the center and the juices run clear, about 5 to 7 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center of the chicken should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Grill peppers until tender, about 2 to 3 minutes per side.'),
('5af34424-4c7e-481a-842a-26fc4e284881', 'ko', 'Remove chicken from the refrigerator and place on the preheated grill with the pepper slices. Cook chicken until no longer pink in the center and the juices run clear, about 5 to 7 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center of the chicken should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Grill peppers until tender, about 2 to 3 minutes per side.'),
('bfd5c1a1-d6fc-475b-8b59-01554a2897a9', 'en', 'Remove chicken and peppers from the grill and allow to cool. Shred chicken and dice peppers.'),
('bfd5c1a1-d6fc-475b-8b59-01554a2897a9', 'ko', 'Remove chicken and peppers from the grill and allow to cool. Shred chicken and dice peppers.'),
('351089cc-59c5-4443-80c5-ca34775005ce', 'en', 'Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onions and garlic; saute until soft, 5 to 7 minutes. Add cooked rice, shredded chicken, diced peppers, diced tomatoes and green chiles, 1/2 of the cheese, and garlic salt; stir until well blended. Cook over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until hot, about 5 minutes.'),
('351089cc-59c5-4443-80c5-ca34775005ce', 'ko', 'Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add onions and garlic; saute until soft, 5 to 7 minutes. Add cooked rice, shredded chicken, diced peppers, diced tomatoes and green chiles, 1/2 of the cheese, and garlic salt; stir until well blended. Cook over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until hot, about 5 minutes.'),
('0397fc7f-e4f2-48e8-8581-fd2660f6b9ca', 'en', 'Spoon rice mixture into the green peppers. Top with remaining cheese.'),
